      "side": 1,
      "message": "See refs in http://shortn/_n6pQMhTKc7\n\nAnd b/227269567\n\nIt\u0027s probably expected that the stubs don\u0027t build by just adding the lib to static_libs, likely because static_libs is not used to compile stubs (or to generate them ?). So this lib needs to be in stub_only_libs to be usable when generating the API stubs (since the @FlaggedApi annotation is part of them).\n\nHowever you still need to have the classes in the implementation library that will be on the bootclasspath, otherwise this is \"dynamically linking\" against a library that isn\u0027t actually on the bootclasspath. It probably still works today because this is just using a constant, which ends up inlined at compile time.\n\nSo I think the lib should also be added to static_libs for framework-connectivity in framework-connectivity-defaults (not framework-connectivity-t as we shouldn\u0027t have it in 2 places, and we\u0027ll need it in framework-connectivity too at some point).\n\nYou can update the comments to explain the situation too :)",
